From c6070548549784c84aa09869ff977bb9f1462f30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:38:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: give the web window its own layout and OSD

The web window loaded the skin's fullscreen video layout and its OSD
action opened the video OSD, so a page showed a seek bar, a time of 0 of
an unknown length and play, pause and seek buttons that mean nothing for
a web view.

Give the window its own empty Estuary layout and add a web OSD, opened
by the OSD action and closed by it again or by Back, with the page's
title and address, history back and forward, reload, and close, which
ends the web view. The client manager keeps what the view a player
asked for reports, so the OSD can show it and enable the history
buttons. Media keys stay with the page, which handles them itself.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
